e category="A" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit></patent-citations><non-patent-citations><nplcit status="new"><text>See also references of EP     1031602A1</text><sources><source name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></nplcit></non-patent-citations></citations></technical-data><parties><applicants><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>IWAMOTO TOMONORI</name><address><country>JP</country> </address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>KANEGAFUCHI CHEMICAL IND</name><address><country>JP</country> </address> </addressbook> </applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SENDA KENICHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>YAMAGUCHI MINORI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>YAMAGUCHI TAKEMA</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>IWAMOTO, TOMONORI</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KANEKA CORPORATION</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SENDA, KENICHI</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>YAMAGUCHI, MINORI</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>YAMAGUCHI, TAKEMA</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>IWAMOTO TOMONORI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SENDA KENICHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>YAMAGUCHI MINORI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>YAMAGUCHI TAKEMA</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>IWAMOTO, TOMONORI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SENDA, KENICHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>YAMAGUCHI, MINORI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>YAMAGUCHI, TAKEMA</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>Pre-expanded polypropylene resin beads which have an expansibility as represented by the following equation of 1.0 to 1.8: Expansibility = [expansion ratio of the beads after steam heating]/[expansion ratio of the beads before steam heating] (wherein the "expansion ratio of the beads after steam heating" is the value of expansion ratio obtained through heating with steam at the melting peak temperature of the base resin determined by examining the beads with a differential scanning calorimeter). The beads can be molded by various in-mold foaming techniques in a reduced cooling time. Thus, a molded object can be stably obtained from the pre-expanded beads which is satisfactory in fusion bonding between the beads and in surface appearance and has no difference in density between the surface and inner parts thereof.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne des grains de résine de polypropylène pré-expansés possédant un pouvoir d'expansion tel que représenté par l'équation suivante de 1,0 sur 1,8 : Pouvoir d'expansion = [coefficient d'expansion des grains après chauffage à la vapeur ]/[coefficient d'expansion des grains avant chauffage à la vapeur] (le  &lt;/=  coefficient d'expansion des grains après chauffage à la vapeur  &gt;/=  représentant la valeur du coefficient d'expansion obtenue par chauffage avec de la vapeur à la température maximale de fusion de la résine de base et déterminée par examen des grains avec un calorimètre à balayage différentiel). On peut mouler les grains au moyen de différentes techniques de moussage dans le moule avec un temps de refroidissement réduit. Ainsi, on peut obtenir de manière stable un objet moulé à partir des grains pré-expansés, ce qui permet d'obtenir une liaison par fusion entre les grains et un aspect de surface satisfaisants, sans qu'il y ait de différence de densité entre la surface et les parties intérieures de l'objet.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>